---
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { getLangFromUrl } from "../../../i18n/utils";

export async function getStaticPaths() {
    return [{ params: { locale: "en" } }, { params: { locale: "it" } }];
}

const locale = getLangFromUrl(Astro.url);

const content = {
    en: {
        title: "JDE → Web: Business Applications",
        subtitle:
            "Rebuilding old JDE workflows as practical, data-heavy web apps",
        period: "Feb - Jun 2024",
        overview:
            "I replaced several clunky JDE screens with web applications that make data work instead of fighting it. The interfaces handle large datasets, let users slice and export information in whatever format they need, and reduce the number of manual workarounds people used to rely on. I also mentored teammates so this approach stuck.",
        challenge:
            "The original JDE screens were hard to use and hard to maintain. They were built for a different era: limited UX patterns, brittle integrations, and no easy way to add new views or exports. Business users needed flexible tools to explore and extract data, not yet another static report.",
        solution:
            "I built React + TypeScript frontends backed by a Java + Spring Boot API. The frontends use configurable data grids with dynamic columns, client-side calculated values, fast server endpoints for large queries, and export features (CSV, Excel, PDF). For heavy data paths we used gRPC to keep latency low. The goal was feature parity first, then cleaner workflows and faster iteration.",
        keyAchievements: [
            {
                title: "Data grids that behave",
                description:
                    "Delivered configurable grids with dynamic columns, fast filtering, and sensible pagination so users can actually work with 10k+ rows without endless scrolling.",
            },
            {
                title: "Exports that don't lie",
                description:
                    "Implemented CSV/Excel/PDF exports that preserve formatting and calculated fields so downstream reports no longer need manual fixes.",
            },
            {
                title: "Faster client-server paths",
                description:
                    "Used gRPC where it mattered to reduce request times for large, repeated queries—users noticed the difference during day-to-day tasks.",
            },
            {
                title: "Practical mentoring",
                description:
                    "Mentored a junior developer on React and TypeScript. We shipped patterns and code examples, not just guidance, so the team could continue the work.",
            },
            {
                title: "Smooth migration",
                description:
                    "Migrated features from the XML-based UI to the web apps without breaking workflows; the product teams could swap components incrementally.",
            },
        ],
        technologies: [
            { name: "React", proficiency: "Expert" },
            { name: "TypeScript", proficiency: "Expert" },
            { name: "Java", proficiency: "Advanced" },
            { name: "Spring Boot", proficiency: "Advanced" },
            { name: "gRPC", proficiency: "Advanced" },
            { name: "PostgreSQL", proficiency: "Intermediate" },
        ],
        techStack: {
            title: "Technical stack",
            items: [
                {
                    category: "Frontend",
                    items: ["React", "TypeScript", "TanStack Table"],
                },
                {
                    category: "Styling & Components",
                    items: ["TailwindCSS", "Shadcn UI"],
                },
                {
                    category: "Backend",
                    items: ["Java", "Spring Boot", "Spring Data"],
                },
                { category: "APIs", items: ["gRPC", "REST"] },
                {
                    category: "Exports",
                    items: ["XLSX", "PDF generation", "CSV"],
                },
                { category: "DevOps", items: ["Docker", "Kubernetes"] },
            ],
        },
        metrics: [
            { label: "Features migrated", value: "15+" },
            { label: "Rows handled", value: "10k+ / view" },
            { label: "Export formats", value: "3" },
            { label: "Development time vs legacy", value: "-50%" },
        ],
    },
    it: {
        title: "JDE → Web: Applicazioni Business",
        subtitle:
            "Reimplementazione di workflow JDE come web app pratiche e orientate ai dati",
        period: "Feb - Giu 2024",
        overview:
            "Ho sostituito diverse schermate JDE scomode con web app che lasciano lavorare i dati, invece di ostacolarli. Le interfacce gestiscono dataset grandi, permettono filtri e export rapidi e riducono i workaround manuali. Ho anche affiancato il team per far sì che il lavoro proseguisse.",
        challenge:
            "Le schermate JDE erano difficili per gli utenti e onerose da mantenere. Erano state pensate per un'epoca diversa: UX limitata, integrazioni fragili e poco spazio per nuove viste o export. Gli utenti chiedevano strumenti flessibili per esplorare e estrarre dati, non report fissi.",
        solution:
            "Ho sviluppato frontend in React + TypeScript e API in Java + Spring Boot. I frontend usano data grid configurabili con colonne dinamiche, valori calcolati lato client, endpoint server performanti per query pesanti e export in CSV, Excel e PDF. Per i percorsi dati più carichi abbiamo usato gRPC per mantenere la latenza bassa. Priorità: feature parity, poi UX più pulita e iterazioni rapide.",
        keyAchievements: [
            {
                title: "Data grid funzionanti",
                description:
                    "Consegna di griglie configurabili con colonne dinamiche, filtri veloci e paginazione sensata: lavorare con oltre 10k righe è diventato pratico.",
            },
            {
                title: "Export affidabili",
                description:
                    "Implementati export CSV/Excel/PDF che preservano formattazione e campi calcolati: nessuna correzione manuale nei report a valle.",
            },
            {
                title: "Percorsi client-server più rapidi",
                description:
                    "Uso di gRPC dove serviva per ridurre i tempi di risposta su query ripetute: gli utenti l'hanno notato nella routine quotidiana.",
            },
            {
                title: "Mentoring pratico",
                description:
                    "Ho affiancato un developer junior su React e TypeScript: abbiamo consegnato esempi e pattern concreti, non solo linee guida.",
            },
            {
                title: "Migrazione graduale",
                description:
                    "Migrazione delle funzionalità dall'interfaccia XML al web senza interrompere i flussi; possibilità di sostituire i componenti passo dopo passo.",
            },
        ],
        technologies: [
            { name: "React", proficiency: "Expert" },
            { name: "TypeScript", proficiency: "Expert" },
            { name: "Java", proficiency: "Avanzato" },
            { name: "Spring Boot", proficiency: "Avanzato" },
            { name: "gRPC", proficiency: "Avanzato" },
            { name: "PostgreSQL", proficiency: "Intermedio" },
        ],
        techStack: {
            title: "Stack tecnico",
            items: [
                {
                    category: "Frontend",
                    items: ["React", "TypeScript", "TanStack Table"],
                },
                {
                    category: "Styling & Components",
                    items: ["TailwindCSS", "Shadcn UI"],
                },
                {
                    category: "Backend",
                    items: ["Java", "Spring Boot", "Spring Data"],
                },
                { category: "APIs", items: ["gRPC", "REST"] },
                {
                    category: "Export",
                    items: ["XLSX", "PDF generation", "CSV"],
                },
                { category: "DevOps", items: ["Docker", "Kubernetes"] },
            ],
        },
        metrics: [
            { label: "Feature migrate", value: "15+" },
            { label: "Righe gestite", value: "10k+ / vista" },
            { label: "Formati export", value: "3" },
            { label: "Tempo sviluppo vs legacy", value: "-50%" },
        ],
    },
};

const page = content[locale];
---

<BaseLayout>
    <div
        class="min-h-screen bg-primary dark:bg-secondary text-secondary dark:text-primary"
    >
        <!-- Hero Section -->
        <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-8 py-20">
            <div class="mb-4">
                <span
                    class="text-sm font-medium text-secondary/60 dark:text-primary/60"
                    >{page.period}</span
                >
            </div>
            <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold mb-4">{page.title}</h1>
            <p class="text-xl text-secondary/80 dark:text-primary/80 mb-8">
                {page.subtitle}
            </p>
            <p
                class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-secondary/75 dark:text-primary/75"
            >
                {page.overview}
            </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Challenge & Solution -->
        <div
            class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-8 py-16 border-t border-secondary/20 dark:border-primary/20"
        >
            <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12">
                <div>
                    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">
                        {locale === "it" ? "Sfida" : "Challenge"}
                    </h2>
                    <p
                        class="text-secondary/75 dark:text-primary/75 leading-relaxed"
                    >
                        {page.challenge}
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">
                        {locale === "it" ? "Soluzione" : "Solution"}
                    </h2>
                    <p
                        class="text-secondary/75 dark:text-primary/75 leading-relaxed"
                    >
                        {page.solution}
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Key Achievements -->
        <div
            class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-8 py-16 border-t border-secondary/20 dark:border-primary/20"
        >
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold mb-8">
                {locale === "it" ? "Risultati chiave" : "Key achievements"}
            </h2>
            <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
                {
                    page.keyAchievements.map((achievement) => (
                        <div class="border-l-2 border-secondary/30 dark:border-primary/30 pl-6 py-2">
                            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">
                                {achievement.title}
                            </h3>
                            <p class="text-secondary/70 dark:text-primary/70 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                                {achievement.description}
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    ))
                }
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Metrics -->
        <div
            class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-8 py-16 border-t border-secondary/20 dark:border-primary/20"
        >
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold mb-8">
                {locale === "it" ? "Impatto" : "Impact"}
            </h2>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-6">
                {
                    page.metrics.map((metric) => (
                        <div class="text-center">
                            <p class="text-4xl font-bold text-secondary dark:text-primary mb-2">
                                {metric.value}
                            </p>
                            <p class="text-sm text-secondary/60 dark:text-primary/60">
                                {metric.label}
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    ))
                }
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Tech Stack -->
        <div
            class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-8 py-16 border-t border-secondary/20 dark:border-primary/20"
        >
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold mb-8">{page.techStack.title}</h2>
            <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
                {
                    page.techStack.items.map((section) => (
                        <div>
                            <h3 class="font-semibold text-lg mb-3 text-secondary dark:text-primary">
                                {section.category}
                            </h3>
                            <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
                                {section.items.map((item) => (
                                    <span class="px-3 py-1 text-sm bg-secondary/10 dark:bg-primary/10 rounded-full text-secondary dark:text-primary">
                                        {item}
                                    </span>
                                ))}
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    ))
                }
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Technologies -->
        <div
            class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-8 py-16 border-t border-secondary/20 dark:border-primary/20"
        >
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold mb-8">
                {locale === "it" ? "Tecnologie usate" : "Technologies used"}
            </h2>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
                {
                    page.technologies.map((tech) => (
                        <div class="p-4 border border-secondary/20 dark:border-primary/20 rounded-lg">
                            <p class="font-medium text-secondary dark:text-primary">
                                {tech.name}
                            </p>
                            <p class="text-sm text-secondary/60 dark:text-primary/60">
                                {tech.proficiency}
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    ))
                }
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Learnings -->
        <div
            class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-8 py-16 border-t border-secondary/20 dark:border-primary/20 mb-20"
        >
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold mb-4">
                {locale === "it" ? "Lezioni chiave" : "Key learnings"}
            </h2>
            <ul class="space-y-3 text-secondary/75 dark:text-primary/75">
                <li class="flex gap-3">
                    <span class="text-secondary dark:text-primary">▸</span>
                    <span
                        >{
                            locale === "it"
                                ? "Spesso è meglio piccoli miglioramenti continui rispetto a un'unica riscrittura mastodontica."
                                : "Small, continuous improvements often beat one giant rewrite."
                        }</span
                    >
                </li>
                <li class="flex gap-3">
                    <span class="text-secondary dark:text-primary">▸</span>
                    <span
                        >{
                            locale === "it"
                                ? "Coinvolgere gli utenti finali sulle prime versioni evita grandi ritorni sui requisiti."
                                : "Involving end users early prevents big rework later."
                        }</span
                    >
                </li>
                <li class="flex gap-3">
                    <span class="text-secondary dark:text-primary">▸</span>
                    <span
                        >{
                            locale === "it"
                                ? "Gli strumenti giusti (griglie configurabili, export affidabili) cambiano il modo in cui i team lavorano, non solo l'interfaccia."
                                : "The right tools—configurable grids and reliable exports—change how teams work, not just the UI."
                        }</span
                    >
                </li>
                <li class="flex gap-3">
                    <span class="text-secondary dark:text-primary">▸</span>
                    <span
                        >{
                            locale === "it"
                                ? "Mentoring pratico lascia un'eredità più duratura di documentazione astratta."
                                : "Practical mentoring leaves a longer-lasting impact than abstract docs."
                        }</span
                    >
                </li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>
</BaseLayout>
